App concept is like an open anonymous story community, not a “send me anonymous messages” app where one person receives messages privately.

The difference:

Existing style (like the image)

One person creates a profile/link.
Other people send anonymous messages to that person.
The owner controls the conversation.
The anonymous person is only a sender.

Your app idea

A person posts an anonymous story, and the whole community interacts with it.

Example:

Anonymous Story

“I’ve been pretending I’m happy at university, but I feel completely lost. I don’t know who to talk to.”

Nobody knows who posted it.

Then the community comments:

“I went through the same thing. You’re not alone.”
“Try talking to someone you trust.”
“This happened to me during my first year too.”

The original poster can reply while staying anonymous.


Key features

1. Anonymous identity system

The person is hidden:

No real name
No profile picture
No followers
No public identity

Instead, the app gives them a random identity:

Example:

“SilentRiver42”
“BlueMoon87”
“HiddenVoice21”

The identity stays consistent only inside that conversation so people know they are replying to the same person.


2. Community-driven stories

Stories appear in a feed:

Categories:

Relationships
Family
School
Work
Confessions
Advice
Life experiences

People vote or react:

❤️ Support
💭 Advice
🤝 Relate


3. The poster stays discreet

The poster should not reveal themselves accidentally.

Protection:

No location sharing
No contacts
No follower system
No private messages by default
Warning when writing identifiable information

Example:

Before posting:

“Your story mentions your workplace and city. Remove details to stay anonymous?”

4. Healthy anonymous discussion

Because anonymity can become toxic, the app needs rules:

Allowed:
✅ Personal experiences
✅ Honest opinions
✅ Asking for advice
✅ Sharing struggles

Not allowed:
❌ Naming private individuals
❌ Doxxing
❌ Threats
❌ Harassment
❌ Sharing private information


5. Optional “proof of humanity”

To reduce bots and abuse:

Account verification behind the scenes
The public stays anonymous
AI moderation detects harmful content


The core idea:

“A place where people can tell their stories without being judged by who they are, and a community responds based on the story itself — not the person behind it.”

It is closer to a mix of Reddit + anonymous confessions + support community, but designed so anonymity protects people instead of creating chaos.